0..75 Comment "//! A flow at a universe above the smallest: the codes it relates are large"
76..154 Comment "//! types, which pack a type in a field, so they live one level up and so does"
155..233 Comment "//! the flow between them. The classifier `Flow[.A = Type[+, 1]](A, B)` is the"
234..267 Comment "//! directed hom of that universe"
268..339 Comment "//! [Gratzer-2026-directed_univalence_simplicial_homotopy_type_theory],"
340..419 Comment "//! Definition 1.2. It stands at its level as `Path` stands at every level. The"
420..491 Comment "//! kernel replays each declaration here at its flow over the level-one"
492..567 Comment "//! universe. A transport or a ride along a path or a flow at that universe"
568..645 Comment "//! reads its motive\'s binder there too, so the motive\'s body decodes a large"
646..668 Comment "//! code at level one."
669..672 Comment "//!"
673..689 Comment "//! - see: #1628"
690..706 Comment "//! - see: #1837"
707..786 Comment "//! - cites: [Gratzer-2026-directed_univalence_simplicial_homotopy_type_theory]"
787..790 Comment "//!"
